$Module harden 3 "Abort TLS when no matching certificate"

DESCRIPTION
===========

The ``harden`` vmod aborts the TLS handshake when there is no server
certificate matching the client's SNI.  Varnish uses the last declared
certificate as fallback when no cert matches SNI; this VMOD ensures
that the fallback is not used for a different hostname or IP by
registering a certificate callback on every ``SSL_CTX``.  If the client
sends no SNI, or if the cert (including fallback) does not match the
requested hostname or IP address, the connection is aborted.  Both hostname and IP address
certificates (SAN dNSName and iPAddress) are supported.

At VCL warm time the VMOD registers an OpenSSL ``SSL_CTX`` ex_data index
whose ``new_func`` installs ``SSL_CTX_set_tlsext_servername_callback``
(to abort when the client sends no SNI) and ``SSL_CTX_set_cert_cb`` (to
abort when the selected certificate does not match the SNI hostname or IP).

$Event event
